-
-Cover the five review perspectives below, using independent subagents in parallel when available. Each required perspective must have adequate evidence and the required independence for the review to pass. If even one finds a verified defect, the review fails; a missing perspective is INCONCLUSIVE, not a defect. Explicit user or project requirements for separate independent reviewers remain binding.
